{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And I will call to witness.</b> Some say the alef is in place of heh, and others said that a future tense came in place of past, and it is possible that ואעידה is according to its plain sense — that I will summon witnesses for myself — and the prophet did what HaShem commanded, even if it is not mentioned:" "<b>Uriah the priest.</b> He was high priest in those days; Zechariah too was a great man. And the way of derash is well known regarding the prophecy of Zechariah the prophet and Uriah the prophet:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:52:44.321930020Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}